                like and what the work helped them achieve.”
              </blockquote>
              <div class="review-author">
                <div class="avatar avatar-purple">A</div>
                <div>
                  <strong>Client name</strong>
                  <span>Brand identity project</span>
                </div>
                <span class="review-quote-mark">↗</span>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article class="review-card review-card-featured">
              <div class="review-stars" aria-label="Five star placeholder">★★★★★</div>
              <blockquote>
                “Replace this placeholder with an authentic testimonial
                about communication, creative thinking, and the final
                design experience.”
              </blockquote>
              <div class="review-author">
                <div class="avatar avatar-blue">B</div>
                <div>
                  <strong>Client name</strong>
                  <span>Digital design project</span>
                </div>
                <span class="review-quote-mark">↗</span>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="disclaimer-note">
            Testimonials above are placeholders, not actual client
            endorsements. Add genuine reviews and obtain permission to
            publish them.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- CONTACT -->
        <section class="contact section-wrap section-spacing" id="contact">
          <div class="contact-panel">
            <div class="contact-decoration contact-decoration-one"></div>
            <div class="contact-decoration contact-decoration-two"></div>

            <div class="contact-inner">
              <span class="contact-eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> HAVE SOMETHING IN MIND?</span>
              <h2>
                Let's make<br />
                <span class="gradient-text">it matter.</span>
              </h2>
              <p>
                Have a big idea, a new business, or a brand ready for its
                next chapter? We'd love to hear about it.
              </p>

              <a class="button button-primary contact-cta" href="mailto:hello@emiratestudios.com">
                Tell us about your project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>

              <div class="contact-bottom">
                <span>GOOD IDEAS START WITH A CONVERSATION.</span>
                <span>EMIRATE STUDIOS © 2026</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>

      <!-- FOOTER -->
      <footer class="site-footer section-wrap">
        <div class="footer-main">
          <a class="brand footer-brand" href="#top" aria-label="Emirate Studios home">
            <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">
              <span></span><span></span><span></span>
            </span>
            <span class="brand-name">emirate<span>®</span><small>STUDIOS</small></span>
          </a>
          <p>Ideas into identity.<br />Design with intention.</p>
          <a class="footer-email" href="mailto:hello@emiratestudios.com">
            hello@emiratestudios.com <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="footer-bottom">
          <span>© 2026 EMIRATE STUDIOS. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED.</span>
          <div class="footer-links">
            <a href="#top">Back to top ↑</a>
            <a href="#work">Selected work</a>
            <a href="#contact">Contact</a>
          </div>
          <span>MADE WITH INTENTION.</span>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </div>

    <script>
      const menuToggle = document.querySelector(".menu-toggle");
      const navigation = document.querySelector(".navigation");

      if (menuToggle && navigation) {
        menuToggle.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const isOpen = menuToggle.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
          menuToggle.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));
          menuToggle.setAttribute(
            "aria-label",
            isOpen ? "Open navigation" : "Close navigation"
          );
          navigation.classList.toggle("is-open", !isOpen);
          document.body.classList.toggle("menu-open", !isOpen);
        });

        navigation.querySelectorAll("a").forEach((link) => {
          link.addEventListener("click", () => {
            menuToggle.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
            menuToggle.setAttribute("aria-label", "Open navigation");
            navigation.classList.remove("is-open");
            document.body.classList.remove("menu-open");
          });
        });
      }

      const filterButtons = document.querySelectorAll(".filter-button");
      const projectCards = document.querySelectorAll(".project-card");

      filterButtons.forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const filter = button.dataset.filter;

          filterButtons.forEach((item) => {
            const active = item === button;
            item.classList.toggle("active", active);
            item.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(active));
          });

          projectCards.forEach((card) => {
            const matches =
              filter === "all" || card.dataset.category === filter;
            card.hidden = !matches;
          });
        });
      });

      const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
        (entries, observer) => {
          entries.forEach((entry) => {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
              observer.unobserve(entry.target);
            }
          });
        },
        { threshold: 0.12 }
      );

      document
        .querySelectorAll(
          ".process-card, .project-card, .service-row, .case-card, .review-card"
        )
        .forEach((element) => {
          element.classList.add("reveal");
          revealObserver.observe(element);
        });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
